<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51424" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴφθῑμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stout, strong</i>, of bodily strength, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤμοις ἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.204
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρατὶ ἐπ᾽ ἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				3.336
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. ποταμῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.749
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῶν ἴ. κάρηνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					23.260
				</span></i>
			; of heroes, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴ. ψυχαί,
			κεφαλαί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				1.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.55
			</span></i>; of Hades, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.534
			</span></i>; also, of women, <i>comely, stately</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. βασίλεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.332
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλοχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.415
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				17.128
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράκοιτις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.92
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυγάτηρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.364
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πηρώ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.287
				</span></i>
			: later, generally, <i>strong, powerful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰφθίμης φιλότητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.P.
					655
				</span></i>
			:—<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> uses <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰφθίμη</span> of women; but
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴφθιμοι ψυχαί, κεφαλαί</span>,
			speaking of men. (No <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝ-</span>; prob. not
			cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴς, ἶφι</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
